        PLUS `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)`

-- "must lodge a return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting -- within 5 months after the end of its financial year": a return lodged
-- before the meeting is not the return the subsection asks for, and one lodged after the last day is late; the text's no on both sides (periods ruling (a); forks F-P5, F-P7).
-- src:17661 | Annual return by companies
-- src:17663 | 197.—(1) Every company, other than a company mentioned in
-- src:17664 | subsection (1A), must lodge a return with the Registrar after its
-- src:17665 | annual general meeting —
-- src:17667 | (a) in the case of a listed company — within 5 months after the
-- src:17668 | end of its financial year; and
-- src:17670 | (b) in any other case — within 7 months after the end of its
-- src:17671 | financial year.
-- src:17675 | (1A) A company having a share capital and keeping a branch
-- src:17676 | register in any place outside Singapore must lodge a return with the
-- src:17677 | Registrar after its annual general meeting —
-- src:17679 | (a) in the case of a listed company — within 6 months after the
-- src:17680 | end of its financial year; and
-- src:17682 | (b) in any other case — within 8 months after the end of its
-- src:17683 | financial year.
-- src:17690 | (1B) The Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks there are special
-- src:17691 | reasons to do so, extend any period within which a company must
-- src:17692 | lodge a return under subsection (1) or (1A) —
-- src:17694 | (a) upon an application by the company; or
-- src:17696 | (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies.
@ref s 197(1) (src:17661-17696)
GIVEN `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the return is lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) the return was lodged after the annual general meeting and within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF     `the day on which the return is lodged` AT LEAST `the day of the annual general meeting`
       AND `the day on which the return is lodged` AT MOST `s 197(1) the last day for lodging the return` `the company is a listed company` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` `the last day of the financial year` `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must lodge a return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting -- (a) ... within 5 months after the end of its financial year" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before the meeting or after the last day the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; forks F-P5, F-P7)

DECLARE `s 197 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 197(1) lodge a return with the Registrar after the annual general meeting`
    `s 197(4) lodge with the Registrar a notice of the date on which the annual general meeting was held`

-- The trace clock counts days after the last day of the financial year (AT 0).
-- src:17661 | Annual return by companies
-- src:17663 | 197.—(1) Every company, other than a company mentioned in
-- src:17664 | subsection (1A), must lodge a return with the Registrar after its
-- src:17665 | annual general meeting —
-- src:17667 | (a) in the case of a listed company — within 5 months after the
-- src:17668 | end of its financial year; and
-- src:17670 | (b) in any other case — within 7 months after the end of its
-- src:17671 | financial year.
-- src:17675 | (1A) A company having a share capital and keeping a branch
-- src:17676 | register in any place outside Singapore must lodge a return with the
-- src:17677 | Registrar after its annual general meeting —
-- src:17679 | (a) in the case of a listed company — within 6 months after the
-- src:17680 | end of its financial year; and
-- src:17682 | (b) in any other case — within 8 months after the end of its
-- src:17683 | financial year.
-- src:17690 | (1B) The Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks there are special
-- src:17691 | reasons to do so, extend any period within which a company must
-- src:17692 | lodge a return under subsection (1) or (1A) —
-- src:17694 | (a) upon an application by the company; or
-- src:17696 | (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies.
@ref s 197(1) (src:17661-17696)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 act`
`s 197(1) a company must lodge a return with the Registrar within the time the subsection gives` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 197(1) lodge a return with the Registrar after the annual general meeting`
    WITHIN `s 197(1) the last day for lodging the return` `the company is a listed company` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` `the last day of the financial year` `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` MINUS `the last day of the financial year`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge its return with the Registrar within the time section 197(1) or (1A) gives"

§ `Section 197(1B): the Registrar may extend the time`

-- "The Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to do so, extend any period ... (a) upon an application by the company; or (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies"
-- A grant gated by "if" and by "upon an application" (split site (ii)): NOTHING when a gate fails (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-G4).
-- src:17690 | (1B) The Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks there are special
-- src:17691 | reasons to do so, extend any period within which a company must
-- src:17692 | lodge a return under subsection (1) or (1A) —
-- src:17694 | (a) upon an application by the company; or
-- src:17696 | (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies.
@ref s 197(1B) (src:17690-17696)
GIVEN `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has applied to the Registrar for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in a prescribed class of companies for which the extension is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1B) the Registrar may extend the period within which the company must lodge its return` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period` AND (`the company has applied to the Registrar for the extension` OR `the company is in a prescribed class of companies for which the extension is made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G4): "extend ... (a) upon an application by the company; or (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies" -- neither "upon an application" nor the prescribed class holds: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to do so, extend" (a power whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G4)

§ `Section 197(2) and (3): what the return must be`

-- src:17700 | (2) The return mentioned in subsections (1) and (1A) —
-- src:17702 | (a) must be in such form;
-- src:17704 | (b) must contain such particulars and information; and
-- src:17706 | (c) must be accompanied by such documents,
-- src:17708 | as may be prescribed.
@ref s 197(2) (src:17700-17708)
GIVEN `the return is in the form prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return contains the particulars and information prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return is accompanied by the documents prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(2) the return is in the form, has the contents and is accompanied by the documents that the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the return is in the form prescribed` AND `the return contains the particulars and information prescribed` AND `the return is accompanied by the documents prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return mentioned in subsections (1) and (1A) (a) must be in such form; (b) must contain such particulars and information; and (c) must be accompanied by such documents, as may be prescribed" (a duty not met; what is prescribed is the regulations' and is taken as three plain facts)

§ `Section 197(4): notice of the date of the annual general meeting held after the return`

-- src:17718 | (4) If a private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold
-- src:17719 | an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its
-- src:17720 | annual return for that financial year, the company must lodge a notice
-- src:17721 | of the date on which the annual general meeting was held with the
-- src:17722 | Registrar within 14 days after that date.
@ref s 197(4) (src:17718-17722)
GIVEN `the private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(4) the private company must lodge a notice of the date on which the annual general meeting was held` MEANS
    IF `the private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year, the company must lodge a notice" (the "If" gate of a duty; fork F-W1)

-- src:17718 | (4) If a private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold
-- src:17719 | an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its
-- src:17720 | annual return for that financial year, the company must lodge a notice
-- src:17721 | of the date on which the annual general meeting was held with the
-- src:17722 | Registrar within 14 days after that date.
@ref s 197(4) (src:17718-17722)
GIVEN `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 197(4) the last day for lodging the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the annual general meeting` 14 Days

-- src:17718 | (4) If a private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold
-- src:17719 | an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its
-- src:17720 | annual return for that financial year, the company must lodge a notice
-- src:17721 | of the date on which the annual general meeting was held with the
-- src:17722 | Registrar within 14 days after that date.
@ref s 197(4) (src:17718-17722)
GIVEN `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice is lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 197(4) the notice was lodged within 14 days` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the day on which the notice is lodged` 14 Days

-- src:17718 | (4) If a private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold
-- src:17719 | an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its
-- src:17720 | annual return for that financial year, the company must lodge a notice
-- src:17721 | of the date on which the annual general meeting was held with the
-- src:17722 | Registrar within 14 days after that date.
@ref s 197(4) (src:17718-17722)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 act`
`s 197(4) a private company must lodge a notice of the date of the annual general meeting within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 197(4) lodge with the Registrar a notice of the date on which the annual general meeting was held`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not lodge a notice of the date of its annual general meeting within 14 days after that date"

§ `Section 197(6): the offence`

-- src:17728 | (6) If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and
-- src:17729 | every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of
-- src:17730 | an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17731 | exceeding $10,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 197(6) (src:17728-17731)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(6) the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with section 197`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- the "If" is unmet

-- src:17728 | (6) If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and
-- src:17729 | every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of
-- src:17730 | an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17731 | exceeding $10,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 197(6) (src:17728-17731)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(6) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with section 197` AND `the officer of the company is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- src:17728 | (6) If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and
-- src:17729 | every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of
-- src:17730 | an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17731 | exceeding $10,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 197(6) (src:17728-17731)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 197(6) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 197(6) the company is guilty of an offence` `the company fails to comply with section 197` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 10000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for those it makes guilty

§ `Section 197: the seam the keel asks (s 4(1) "annual return")`

-- The keel asks: is this return the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)? Subsection (1) is for "every company, other than a company mentioned in
-- subsection (1A)", so a return of a (1A) company is not the return required under (1) on the text's own words (finding 5 and a marginal reading in NOTES.md).
-- src:17661 | Annual return by companies
-- src:17663 | 197.—(1) Every company, other than a company mentioned in
-- src:17664 | subsection (1A), must lodge a return with the Registrar after its
-- src:17665 | annual general meeting —
-- src:17675 | (1A) A company having a share capital and keeping a branch
-- src:17676 | register in any place outside Singapore must lodge a return with the
-- src:17677 | Registrar after its annual general meeting —
@ref s 197(1) (src:17661-17677)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return is lodged with the Registrar after the annual general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) the return is the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)` MEANS
    IF `s 197(1A) the company is one mentioned in subsection (1A)` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 4(1) "“annual return” means the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)" and section 197(1) is for "every company, other than a company mentioned in subsection (1A)" (finding 5)
    ELSE (IF `the return is lodged with the Registrar after the annual general meeting of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must lodge a return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting" -- a return lodged before the meeting is not the one required

§ `Section 198: the financial year of a company`

-- 31 August 2018 is named by the section itself; the core has no name for it.
-- src:17739 | 198.—(1) Where a company is incorporated on or after 31 August
-- src:17740 | 2018 —
@ref s 198(1) (src:17739-17740)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198 the day 31 August 2018` MEANS Date 31 8 2018

-- src:17739 | 198.—(1) Where a company is incorporated on or after 31 August
-- src:17740 | 2018 —
@ref s 198(1) (src:17739-17740)
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(1) the company is incorporated on or after 31 August 2018` MEANS
    IF `the date of incorporation of the company` AT LEAST `s 198 the day 31 August 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is incorporated on or after 31 August 2018" (the "Where" gate of a rule; subsection (3) is for a company incorporated before that date; fork F-W1)

-- src:17764 | (3) Where a company was incorporated before 31 August 2018 —
@ref s 198(3) (src:17764)
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(3) the company was incorporated before 31 August 2018` MEANS
    IF `the date of incorporation of the company` LESS THAN `s 198 the day 31 August 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company was incorporated before 31 August 2018" (the "Where" gate of a rule; subsection (1) is for a company incorporated on or after that date; fork F-W1)

-- (1)(a): the first financial year of a company incorporated on or after 31 August 2018 starts on the date of incorporation and, subject to subsection (4),
-- ends on the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b). A notice under (4) that specifies a new last day replaces it.
-- src:17742 | (a) the company’s first financial year starts on the company’s
-- src:17743 | date of incorporation and, subject to subsection (4), ends
-- src:17748 | on the last day of the company’s first financial year as
-- src:17749 | furnished under section 19(1)(b); and
@ref s 198(1)(a) (src:17742-17749)
GIVEN `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` IS A DATE
      `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new last day specified by that notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198(1)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year` MEANS
    IF `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year`
    THEN `the new last day specified by that notice`
    ELSE `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)`

-- src:17739 | 198.—(1) Where a company is incorporated on or after 31 August
-- src:17740 | 2018 —
-- src:17742 | (a) the company’s first financial year starts on the company’s
-- src:17743 | date of incorporation and, subject to subsection (4), ends
-- src:17748 | on the last day of the company’s first financial year as
-- src:17749 | furnished under section 19(1)(b); and
@ref s 198(1)(a) (src:17739-17749)
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` IS A DATE
      `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new last day specified by that notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(1)(a) the period is the first financial year of the company` MEANS
    IF     `the first day of the period` EQUALS `the date of incorporation of the company`
       AND `the last day of the period` EQUALS `s 198(1)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year` `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` `the new last day specified by that notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company's first financial year starts on the company's date of incorporation and ... ends on the last day of the company's first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)" (a closed statement of which period the first financial year is; fork F-D1)

-- (1)(b) and (3)(b): each subsequent financial year starts immediately after the end of the previous one and ends on the last day of a period of 12 months
-- (or another regular interval the Registrar allows): the period of that many months beginning with the first day (P10).
-- src:17751 | (b) each of the company’s subsequent financial years starts
-- src:17752 | immediately after the end of the previous financial year
-- src:17753 | and ends on the last day of a period of 12 months (or such
-- src:17754 | other regular interval as the Registrar may allow).
@ref s 198(1)(b) (src:17751-17754)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198(1)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the first day of the period` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` Months

-- src:17751 | (b) each of the company’s subsequent financial years starts
-- src:17752 | immediately after the end of the previous financial year
-- src:17753 | and ends on the last day of a period of 12 months (or such
-- src:17754 | other regular interval as the Registrar may allow).
@ref s 198(1)(b) (src:17751-17754)
GIVEN `the last day of the previous financial year` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(1)(b) the period is a subsequent financial year of the company` MEANS
    IF     `the first day of the period` EQUALS `the last day of the previous financial year` PLUS 1
       AND `the last day of the period` EQUALS `s 198(1)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year` `the first day of the period` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each of the company's subsequent financial years starts immediately after the end of the previous financial year and ends on the last day of a period of 12 months (or such other regular interval as the Registrar may allow)" (a closed statement of which periods are subsequent financial years; fork F-D1)

-- (2): the first financial year must not be longer than 18 months unless the Registrar, on the company's application, otherwise approves.
-- src:17758 | (2) A company’s first financial year must not be longer than
-- src:17759 | 18 months unless the Registrar on the application of the company
-- src:17760 | otherwise approves.
@ref s 198(2) (src:17758-17760)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 198(2) the period is longer than 18 months` MEANS
    `the last day of the period` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the first day of the period` 18 Months

-- src:17758 | (2) A company’s first financial year must not be longer than
-- src:17759 | 18 months unless the Registrar on the application of the company
-- src:17760 | otherwise approves.
@ref s 198(2) (src:17758-17760)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar on the application of the company has approved a longer first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(2) the first financial year is no longer than the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 198(2) the period is longer than 18 months` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar on the application of the company has approved a longer first financial year`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's first financial year must not be longer than 18 months unless the Registrar on the application of the company otherwise approves" ("unless" not met). The text names no bearer of the duty, so there is no regulative rule (fork F-B1).

-- (3)(a): a company incorporated before 31 August 2018: the last day of its first financial year ending on or after that date is the anniversary of a day.
-- The anniversary is the first one on or after 31 August 2018; a 29 February steps to 28 February in a year that is not a leap year (subsection (7); P4).
-- src:17766 | (a) the last day of the financial year for the company’s first
-- src:17767 | financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018 is —
-- src:17769 | (i) where the company had, before 31 August 2018,
-- src:17770 | lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification with
-- src:17771 | the Registrar informing the Registrar of the end of
-- src:17772 | the company’s financial year — the anniversary of
-- src:17773 | the last day of the financial year as indicated by the
-- src:17774 | company in the last annual return or last such
-- src:17775 | notification with the Registrar; or
-- src:17777 | (ii) where the company had not, before 31 August 2018,
-- src:17778 | lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification with
-- src:17779 | the Registrar informing the Registrar of the end of
-- src:17780 | the company’s financial year — the anniversary of
-- src:17781 | the date of incorporation of the company; and
-- src:17832 | (7) For the purposes of —
-- src:17834 | (a) subsection (3)(a)(i), where the last day of the financial year
-- src:17835 | of a company as indicated in the last annual return or in the
-- src:17836 | last notification with the Registrar informing the Registrar
-- src:17837 | of the last day of the company’s financial year falls on
-- src:17838 | 29 February, the anniversary of that date in a year that is
-- src:17839 | not a leap year is to be taken as 28 February; and
-- src:17841 | (b) subsection (3)(a)(ii), where the date of incorporation of a
-- src:17842 | company falls on 29 February, the anniversary of that date
-- src:17843 | in a year that is not a leap year is to be taken as 28 February.
@ref s 198(3)(a) (src:17766-17843)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the number of years already stepped` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198(3)(a) the first anniversary on or after 31 August 2018` MEANS
    IF `period: the last day of a period after` `the day` `the number of years already stepped` Years AT LEAST `s 198 the day 31 August 2018`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day` `the number of years already stepped` Years
    ELSE `s 198(3)(a) the first anniversary on or after 31 August 2018` `the day` (`the number of years already stepped` PLUS 1)

-- src:17769 | (i) where the company had, before 31 August 2018,
-- src:17770 | lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification with
-- src:17771 | the Registrar informing the Registrar of the end of
-- src:17772 | the company’s financial year — the anniversary of
-- src:17773 | the last day of the financial year as indicated by the
-- src:17774 | company in the last annual return or last such
-- src:17775 | notification with the Registrar; or
@ref s 198(3)(a)(i) (src:17769-17775)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198(3)(a)(i) the last day of the first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018, where a return or notification had been lodged` MEANS
    `s 198(3)(a) the first anniversary on or after 31 August 2018` `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` 0

-- src:17777 | (ii) where the company had not, before 31 August 2018,
-- src:17778 | lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification with
-- src:17779 | the Registrar informing the Registrar of the end of
-- src:17780 | the company’s financial year — the anniversary of
-- src:17781 | the date of incorporation of the company; and
@ref s 198(3)(a)(ii) (src:17777-17781)
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 198(3)(a)(ii) the last day of the first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018, where none had been lodged` MEANS
    `s 198(3)(a) the first anniversary on or after 31 August 2018` `the date of incorporation of the company` 0

-- src:17766 | (a) the last day of the financial year for the company’s first
-- src:17767 | financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018 is —
-- src:17769 | (i) where the company had, before 31 August 2018,
